1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,998
Thirty-three kilometers off the coast of Brazil, there's a

2
00:00:03,998 --> 00:00:08,133
green island that looks like paradise. Forest, rocks, waves.

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:11,097
But almost nobody is allowed to set foot on

4
00:00:11,097 --> 00:00:14,406
it. Because hidden in the trees are thousands of

5
00:00:14,406 --> 00:00:18,266
venomous snakes that live nowhere else on Earth. Welcome

6
00:00:18,266 --> 00:00:21,919
to Snake Island. Today, we'll separate the facts from

7
00:00:21,919 --> 00:00:25,365
the legends, and see why you'd never survive here.

8
00:00:25,915 --> 00:00:29,350
Welcome to Earth Decoded. If you love the most

9
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:33,606
extreme places on our planet, tap subscribe. Today, we're

10
00:00:33,606 --> 00:00:36,966
going to the island that Brazil won't let you

11
00:00:36,966 --> 00:00:37,414
visit.

12
00:00:37,964 --> 00:00:41,333
Its real name is Ilha da Queimada Grande. It

13
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:46,005
sits in the Atlantic Ocean, about thirty-three kilometers off

14
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:48,225
the coast of São Paulo state.

15
00:00:48,775 --> 00:00:52,718
It's small, only about forty-three hectares, less than half

16
00:00:52,718 --> 00:00:55,858
a square kilometer. You could walk across it in

17
00:00:55,858 --> 00:00:58,598
less than an hour, if it weren't for what

18
00:00:58,598 --> 00:00:59,399
lives there.

19
00:00:59,949 --> 00:01:03,722
Its slopes are covered in humid Atlantic Forest, with

20
00:01:03,722 --> 00:01:07,423
steep rocky cliffs dropping into the sea. There's no

21
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:10,626
beach and no dock. Boats have to approach the

22
00:01:10,626 --> 00:01:14,683
rocks carefully, and landing is dangerous even before you

23
00:01:14,683 --> 00:01:15,608
meet a snake.

24
00:01:16,158 --> 00:01:19,883
Its name means big burned island. Long ago, people

25
00:01:19,883 --> 00:01:23,012
tried to burn the forest to clear land for

26
00:01:23,012 --> 00:01:25,545
farming, but the plan didn't last.

27
00:01:26,095 --> 00:01:29,929
The island belongs to its snakes: the golden lancehead,

28
00:01:29,929 --> 00:01:32,996
a pit viper found only here and nowhere else

29
00:01:32,996 --> 00:01:33,903
in the world.

30
00:01:34,453 --> 00:01:37,912
It grows to around seventy centimeters to a meter

31
00:01:37,912 --> 00:01:41,583
long, with a pale, golden-brown body, which gives it

32
00:01:41,583 --> 00:01:42,218
its name.

33
00:01:42,768 --> 00:01:45,302
So how did snakes end up alone on an

34
00:01:45,302 --> 00:01:48,893
island? About eleven thousand years ago, at the end

35
00:01:48,893 --> 00:01:51,709
of the last ice age, sea levels rose and

36
00:01:51,709 --> 00:01:55,018
cut this hill off from the mainland. The snakes

37
00:01:55,018 --> 00:01:56,848
living there were trapped.

38
00:01:57,398 --> 00:02:00,412
On the island, there were no rats, mice or

39
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:03,354
frogs to eat on the ground. So the snakes

40
00:02:03,354 --> 00:02:06,726
moved up into the trees and started hunting the

41
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:10,027
one thing that kept arriving: migrating birds.

42
00:02:10,577 --> 00:02:14,106
That makes life hard. Most of their food arrives

43
00:02:14,106 --> 00:02:17,562
only when birds stop on the island during their

44
00:02:17,562 --> 00:02:21,974
migrations. Between those seasons, many snakes go hungry for

45
00:02:21,974 --> 00:02:22,929
long periods.

46
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:26,637
Quick question. Are you more afraid of snakes or

47
00:02:26,637 --> 00:02:29,005
of spiders? Tell me in the comments.

48
00:02:29,555 --> 00:02:32,713
Hunting birds is hard. If a snake bites a

49
00:02:32,713 --> 00:02:35,949
bird and it flies away, it's gone. So over

50
00:02:35,949 --> 00:02:40,956
thousands of years, the golden lancehead's venom became extremely

51
00:02:40,956 --> 00:02:44,808
fast-acting, able to kill a bird almost instantly.

52
00:02:45,358 --> 00:02:49,153
Scientists believe its venom is more potent than that

53
00:02:49,153 --> 00:02:53,449
of its mainland relative, the jararaca, which already causes

54
00:02:53,449 --> 00:02:55,811
many of the snakebites in Brazil.

55
00:02:56,361 --> 00:03:00,255
Venom from these vipers attacks the blood and tissue.

56
00:03:00,255 --> 00:03:04,443
A bite can cause intense pain, swelling, bleeding, kidney

57
00:03:04,443 --> 00:03:08,337
damage and tissue death. Without antivenom, it can be

58
00:03:08,337 --> 00:03:08,777
fatal.

59
00:03:09,327 --> 00:03:13,136
Snakebites are a real problem in Brazil. The country

60
00:03:13,136 --> 00:03:17,237
records tens of thousands of snakebite cases every year,

61
00:03:17,237 --> 00:03:21,338
most of them from mainland lanceheads like the jararaca.

62
00:03:21,888 --> 00:03:25,116
Doctors say that after a bite, you should stay

63
00:03:25,116 --> 00:03:28,415
as calm and still as possible, remove rings and

64
00:03:28,415 --> 00:03:31,853
tight clothing, and get to a hospital fast. Don't

65
00:03:31,853 --> 00:03:34,660
cut the wound, don't try to suck out the

66
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:37,397
venom and don't use a tight tourniquet.

67
00:03:37,947 --> 00:03:41,871
And here's the problem. On Snake Island, there's no

68
00:03:41,871 --> 00:03:46,026
hospital, no doctor and no road. The nearest antivenom

69
00:03:46,026 --> 00:03:48,796
is hours away by boat and car on the

70
00:03:48,796 --> 00:03:49,489
mainland.

71
00:03:50,039 --> 00:03:52,646
And the snakes are hard to see. They rest

72
00:03:52,646 --> 00:03:55,572
on branches and among leaves at about head and

73
00:03:55,572 --> 00:03:59,451
hand height, exactly where you'd reach while climbing through

74
00:03:59,451 --> 00:04:00,151
the forest.

75
00:04:00,701 --> 00:04:04,571
Researchers who visit wear thick boots and leg guards,

76
00:04:04,571 --> 00:04:08,369
move slowly, and watch every branch before they touch

77
00:04:08,369 --> 00:04:11,737
it. Even experts treat every step on the island

78
00:04:11,737 --> 00:04:12,669
with respect.

79
00:04:13,219 --> 00:04:16,632
Now, the legends. You may have heard there's one

80
00:04:16,632 --> 00:04:20,188
snake for every square meter. That's a myth. Early

81
00:04:20,188 --> 00:04:22,605
estimates were wildly exaggerated.

82
00:04:23,155 --> 00:04:27,875
Modern studies by Brazilian scientists estimate the population at

83
00:04:27,875 --> 00:04:31,650
a few thousand snakes, roughly two to four thousand,

84
00:04:31,650 --> 00:04:35,208
which is still an incredibly high number for such

85
00:04:35,208 --> 00:04:36,297
a small island.

86
00:04:36,847 --> 00:04:40,245
There's also a famous legend that the island's last

87
00:04:40,245 --> 00:04:43,843
lighthouse keeper and his family were killed by snakes

88
00:04:43,843 --> 00:04:46,774
that came in through a window. It's a creepy

89
00:04:46,774 --> 00:04:50,372
story, but there's no solid evidence it ever happened.

90
00:04:50,922 --> 00:04:54,858
What is true: the lighthouse was automated decades ago,

91
00:04:54,858 --> 00:04:57,578
so nobody needs to live there anymore.

92
00:04:58,128 --> 00:05:00,608
Have you ever heard a scary legend about a

93
00:05:00,608 --> 00:05:02,971
place near you? Tell me in the comments.

94
00:05:03,521 --> 00:05:08,441
Today, Brazil's navy and environmental authorities forbid visits to

95
00:05:08,441 --> 00:05:12,481
the island. Only scientists and navy crews with special

96
00:05:12,481 --> 00:05:16,447
permission can land, and researchers usually go with a

97
00:05:16,447 --> 00:05:16,961
doctor.

98
00:05:17,511 --> 00:05:20,751
The ban isn't only to protect people. It's to

99
00:05:20,751 --> 00:05:24,568
protect the snakes. The golden lancehead is listed as

100
00:05:24,568 --> 00:05:28,745
critically endangered, because it lives on one tiny island

101
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:29,969
and nowhere else.

102
00:05:30,519 --> 00:05:34,315
One of the biggest threats is illegal collection. Wildlife

103
00:05:34,315 --> 00:05:37,849
smugglers have sneaked onto the island to catch snakes

104
00:05:37,849 --> 00:05:41,253
for collectors, who can pay thousands of dollars for

105
00:05:41,253 --> 00:05:42,103
a single one.

106
00:05:42,653 --> 00:05:46,202
It's not the only island like this in Brazil.

107
00:05:46,202 --> 00:05:50,302
On Alcatrazes, another island off São Paulo, lives a

108
00:05:50,302 --> 00:05:55,112
different viper found nowhere else, the Alcatrazes lancehead.

109
00:05:55,662 --> 00:05:59,388
Fire, disease and the small size of the population

110
00:05:59,388 --> 00:06:03,263
also put them at risk. Because they've been isolated

111
00:06:03,263 --> 00:06:06,841
so long, the snakes have little genetic variety.

112
00:06:07,391 --> 00:06:11,828
And scientists want them protected for another reason: venom

113
00:06:11,828 --> 00:06:15,081
can save lives. Research on the venom of the

114
00:06:15,081 --> 00:06:19,444
mainland jararaca helped create captopril, one of the first

115
00:06:19,444 --> 00:06:23,881
modern blood pressure medicines, used by millions of people.

116
00:06:24,431 --> 00:06:29,049
Brazil's Butantan Institute in São Paulo studies these snakes

117
00:06:29,049 --> 00:06:33,440
and produces antivenom that saves thousands of lives every

118
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:33,818
year.

119
00:06:34,368 --> 00:06:38,053
Golden lancehead venom is being studied too, for its

120
00:06:38,053 --> 00:06:41,525
effects on blood clotting and the heart. A deadly

121
00:06:41,525 --> 00:06:44,501
snake could one day lead to new medicines.

122
00:06:45,051 --> 00:06:48,608
So, could you survive Snake Island? If you landed

123
00:06:48,608 --> 00:06:52,238
there alone and got bitten, with hours between you

124
00:06:52,238 --> 00:06:56,376
and antivenom, your chances would be poor. That's exactly

125
00:06:56,376 --> 00:07:00,731
why nobody goes without permission, experience and a doctor.

126
00:07:01,281 --> 00:07:04,376
But the island isn't a monster's lair. It's a

127
00:07:04,376 --> 00:07:08,227
tiny, fragile world, and the snakes need protection from

128
00:07:08,227 --> 00:07:11,116
us more than we need protection from them.

129
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:15,635
Last question. Which extreme place should we explore next?

130
00:07:15,635 --> 00:07:17,277
Tell me in the comments.

131
00:07:17,827 --> 00:07:21,520
Thanks for watching Earth Decoded. If you enjoyed this,

132
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:24,608
like the video, subscribe, and share it with a

133
00:07:24,608 --> 00:07:27,428
friend who is scared of snakes. See you in

134
00:07:27,428 --> 00:07:28,301
the next one.

